{title: The Strife Is O'er}
{artist: Anon. Latin; tr. Francis Pott}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: the-strife-is-oer.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]The strife is o'er, the [D]battle done
[G]The victory of [C]life is [D]won
[G]The song of tri[D]umph has be[Em]gun
[C]Al__[G]__le__[D]__lu__[G]__ia
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]The powers of death have [D]done their worst
[G]But Christ their legions [C]hath dis[D]persed
[G]Let shouts of ho[D]ly joy out[Em]burst
[C]Al__[G]__le__[D]__lu__[G]__ia
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]The three sad days have [D]quickly sped
[G]He rises glorious [C]from the [D]dead
[G]All glory to our [D]risen [Em]Head
[C]Al__[G]__le__[D]__lu__[G]__ia
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]He broke the age-bound [D]chains of hell
[G]The bars from heaven's [C]high por[D]tals fell
[G]Let hymns of praise His [D]triumph [Em]tell
[C]Al__[G]__le__[D]__lu__[G]__ia
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Lord, by the stripes which [D]wounded Thee
[G]From death's dread sting Thy [C]servants [D]free
[G]That we may live and [D]sing to [Em]Thee
[C]Al__[G]__le__[D]__lu__[G]__ia
{end_of_verse}
